            <ArticleTitle>Headache in a case of Rhupus syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>155-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1526-4610.2007.00981.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of Rhupus with secondary anti-phospholipid syndrome who presented with headache and papilloedema due to cerebral venous thrombosis. We propose that an increased awareness about the condition and meticulous investigation of headaches in lupus can avert catastrophic outcomes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
